From 1238ea1bf5fd8c863ca3e3c24bedef3afbe6b713 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Demand the provenance attestation rather than hope for it

npm generates provenance for an OIDC publish and for nothing else, so
the attestation is what tells a consumer this tarball came from this
repository's workflow. But npm only turns it on by itself, and the
auto-enable is conditional and silent: lib/utils/oidc.js requires that
`provenance` is still at its default, that the runner is not CircleCI,
that the forge is GitHub Actions with a public repository_visibility
claim, and that the registry reports the package public -- all inside a
try/catch that logs at verbose level and returns. Any of those failing
produces an unattested publish with every step green.

`--provenance` asks for it explicitly, and npm fails the publish rather
than dropping it when it cannot be generated. For a package whose whole
job is verifying evidence, a missing attestation should stop the
release, not pass it.

Remove patch/provenance-explicit.patch and its row in patch/README.md
in the commit that applies this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W4X2MprZjtGPiBVth8jTrW
---
 .github/workflows/publish.yml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/publish.yml b/.github/workflows/publish.yml
index 66a5b22..8978e8d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/publish.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/publish.yml
@@ -143,7 +143,7 @@ jobs:
             *-*) DIST=next ;;
             *)   DIST=latest ;;
           esac
-          npm publish --access public --tag "$DIST"
+          npm publish --access public --provenance --tag "$DIST"
 
   tag:
     name: tag
-- 
